    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green \u2014 12 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `initials` field is a derived, read-only property on the owner response, so I followed the existing pattern used for `displayName`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits `getInitials`/`setInitials` on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n       + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n   This produces the upper-cased first letters, dot-separated with a trailing dot (`\"john\"` + `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`).\n\nThe `RespondWithOwner` OfficeFloor function already maps the entity through `OwnerMapper`, so both the `GET /api/owners/{id}` and create responses now carry `initials` with no wiring changes needed.",
